! Original OpenSwing two-axis elastic rotor-mount benchmark. SI input units.
! Use zero gravity, alpha=beta=0, fixed modal frame, Mach=0 and 4 modes.
! Speed 10 m/s is stable; 14 m/s has an unstable whirl pair.
! The root is clamped; the tip is pinned in translation and free in rotation.
! EIcc=EInn=5 N m2, L=1 m, Iyy=Izz=.2 kg m2, Hx=-1.8 kg m2/s.
! Axial stiffness is finite to avoid redundant axial support reactions.
! Engine 1: ideal zero-thrust rotor, Omega=180 rad/s about the -x thrust axis.
! Blade integrals: 3 blades, constant .06 m chord, R=.5 m; inflow angles at 10 m/s.
! Those inflow-angle integrals stay fixed in a speed sweep, as in Engine type 2.
! Negative Rdisk disables its jet. Rotor inertia/spin are in Weight, not Engine.
! Engine 2/3 settings apply unit y/z torques in N m for response checks.
